Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Gauge Six Moves Before the Kick

Story & Context: The debut opens at 128 BPM with no kick. Lowri bows one open crwth fifth while gradually increasing pressure. The bridge-contact channel becomes rougher until a mechanical dial beside the preamp crosses a marked position labeled six. Only then does Ife trigger the first low kick. The kick is therefore late relative to a conventional downbeat but exact relative to the physical gesture. On the next cycle the same threshold triggers a tenor rototom instead, proving that the cue belongs to force rather than a particular instrument.

Mara enters every fourth cycle with a prepared clavichord octave immediately after the bow pressure drops. Nia remains silent for nearly a minute, then adds one cup-muted low fifth after Lowri’s longest release. As the track develops, the threshold is not changed; Lowri simply reaches it faster, compressing the rhythmic response without altering BPM.

The final sixteen bars remove electronic sub and leave crwth contact impulse, kick, rototom, and one clavichord anchor. Lowri deliberately stops just below the marked threshold on the last bow stroke. No final kick arrives.

